ich originally come  from norse mythology were giant humanoid  creatures of a men's size sometimes  growing as tall as 12 feet and weighing  up to one tonne  it's also worth mentioning that there  are several different subspecies of  troll including forest trolls mountain  trolls river trolls and the troll of  nadrage a troll subspecies with  disproportionately large hands  controls are incredibly dangerous  unpredictable violent and aggressive  creatures that have a taste for human  flesh  making them particularly terrifying  we see trolls in the trailer for  hogwarts legacy and i'm willing to bet  that we're going to need to use some  magic to confiscate those gigantic clubs  3. thestrals  ethestrel is a breed of winged horse  that possesses skeletal and reptilian  features resembling a sort of evil  pegasus  they have dragon-like heads pupilless  white eyes and vast black leathery wings  the ministry of magic considers  thestrals to be dangerous and they have  a bad rap as omens of misfortune because  they are only visible to those who have  seen death  we don't actually see thestrals until  the state of play that is but at one  point in the hogwarts legacy trailer we  see a flying carriage being magically  lifted into the air if you're any sort  of harry potter fan at all then you'll  know that thestrals are responsible  for mer people  mer people are sentient magical beasts  that live underwater and can be found  all over the world  they are certainly mysterious creatures  that we don't get to know very well in  the story only playing a relatively  small role  outside of hogwarts they reside in the  black lake and we only really see them  during the events of the second task of  the tri-wizard tournament where they  agreed to keep four people in an  enchanted sleep in their village for an  hour protecting them until they are  saved by their respective champion  provided that the lake near hogwarts is  featured in the trailer for hogwarts  legacy and that the lake is such an  important part of the school grounds i  suspect it's highly likely that we'll  encounter more people there  5. hippogriffs hippogriffs are magical  beasts that have the front legs wings  and head of a giant eagle and the body  behind legs and tail of a horse  one notable hippogriff in harry potter  was of course buckbeak who harry and  hermione helped save from execution in  1994  the game trailers feature hippogriffs on  a few occasions  so i'm positive that we're going to get  to experience them in game who knows  maybe we'll even run into them in the  care of magical creatures class 6.  acromantulas  acromanculars are basically giant  spiders if you remember the most notable  acromancular from the series is aragog  hagrid's old pet and the reason for his  expulsion from hogwarts acromantulas are  classified as a category 5x beast by the  ministry of magic and this is for good  reason it has been expressed that the  leg span of acromanculars can be as  large as 15 feet which makes them a bit  more intimidating than your average  house spider in the trailer we see a  hogwarts student fighting off an  acromantula and though we can say for  sure that this one wasn't aragog because  of the date the game is set in it  doesn't mean that there weren't others  living in the forbidden forest at the  time  seven dementors dementors are cloaked  creatures three meters tall with dark  grey scabby skin they are truly foul  creatures that represent unhappiness and  despair and they are frequently known to  be the guards of azkaban prison ensuring  that all the darkest witches and wizards  inside do not escape  dementors can strip you of your soul and  leave you just a shell of a person and  that kind of power can't be ignored  however their achilles heel is the  patronus charm as it is a positive light  force that represents everything that  they aren't as a result they are  repelled by its presence  this means that as long as the witch  wizard knows how to use a patronus charm  then they are safe from dementors  provided that one confirmed aspect of  hogwarts legacy is figuring out your  player's patronus i'm willing to bet  that we'll have to use them against  dementors at one point or another eight  in ferry the inferi or nefarious  singular is effectively a corpse that  has been reanimated by a dark wizard's  curse  according to pottermore the inferius  becomes a grizzly puppet used as an  expendable servant by a dark wizard  adding that an inferius can be spotted  by its white and cloudy eyes  harry and dumbledore are famously  attacked by inferi in the cave when  trying to retrieve one of voldemort's  horcruxes  and ferry are front and center in the  hogwarts legacy trailer so i can't wait  to see when we'll encounter them perhaps  we'll learn some sort of fire spell to  ward them off the homage to dumbledore  nine boggarts boggarts are essentially  manifestations of our deepest darkest  fears they are immortal shape-shifting  non-beings that transform into whatever  you fear most  no one knows what the pocket looks like  by itself because it will transform as  soon as you encounter it when buckets  aren't scaring people they can usually  be found to rustling around in confined  spaces all lurking around dark corners  boggarts are the perfect tool to keep  players on their toes and given that our  characters will enroll in defense  against the dark arts classes it's  inevitable that we're going to face a  boggart or two  i wonder if character customization will  allow us to choose our boggart  10. moon carves the moon calf was a shy  magical beast that only came out of its  burrow during a full moon  the moon calf had smooth pale gray skin  and four spindly legs that ended in  large flat webbed feet the moon calf  also had a very long neck and bulging  blue eyes that sat on the top of its  head  though the mooncarve was first brought  to our attention in fantastic beasts it  doesn't mean that the mooncalf's  presence 